## 2026-09-30

### Local usage collection, an optional billing meter, and HARD REFRESH (#16)

**TechLuddite** · GitHub [@TechLuddite](https://github.com/TechLuddite) · X [@gh_TechLuddite](https://x.com/gh_TechLuddite)

HARD REFRESH is the first chip in the module strip, with IPC for the desk and
the overlay; it bypasses the GitHub, external-IP and Grok billing caches. Grok
token totals now come from Grok's own local session files when Omarchy has no
record for it, and USAGE renders each provider as its own tinted block.

The whole 09-18 review came back as one commit per item, and all of it checks out
here:
- Both outbound paths are opt-in now, enable flags instead of skip flags:
  `INFOMARCHY_ALLOW_GROK_BILLING=1` and `INFOMARCHY_ALLOW_CLAUDE_REFRESH=1`.
  Nothing spends against an AI account unless asked.
- Both are gated on the USAGE card being on screen, passed as the `--usage-visible`
  argv flag rather than an environment variable, so an inherited environment cannot
  claim the card is visible. Proven live: flag alone is false, card alone is false,
  both together is true.
- HARD REFRESH no longer bypasses the Claude spend throttle. Forcing skips caches,
  never the limiter, and a forced Grok billing fetch still waits 10 seconds.
- The declarative collector command is back, so a future `collector.running = true`
  cannot silently drop `--demo`, and the unreachable return in
  `grokCliAccessToken()` is gone.

477 tests pass on the merged tree. Fourth contribution from this author.

## 2026-09-22

### Event-driven refresh on top of the poll (#39)

**Reverb** · GitHub [@reverb256](https://github.com/reverb256) · X: none found (checked 2026-09-18, see Backfill)

The follow-up Fred invited on #11, built to the constraints he set there: the
repeating timer stays as the floor, and paths come from HOME, HERMES_HOME and
XDG_STATE_HOME with no literal home directory. A change to Hermes's state.db or
WAL, or to dashboard.json, pulls the next refresh forward after 250 ms.

Fixed in the merge: FileView preloads by default, which would have read gus's
12 MB state.db and 1 MB WAL into memory in every desk instance only to watch
them. Adding `preload: false` keeps them as pure watches. A throwaway quickshell
confirmed the change signal still fires on append and atomic replace without
loading the file. Dropped `atomicWrites` from the dashboard.json watcher,
since it only affects writes and this FileView never writes.

435 tests pass on the merged tree. Second contribution (after #11).

### Pin the desk to one workspace, keeping the wallpaper on all of them (#38)

**Casey Shields** · GitHub [@shieldsworks](https://github.com/shieldsworks) · X: none found (checked 2026-09-22)

`omarchy-shell infomarchy setDeskWorkspace 5` shows the cards only while
workspace 5 is on screen. The wallpaper still draws everywhere, because the gate
sits on the cards and not the background surface. `0` (the default) means every
workspace, so an install that never sets it behaves exactly as before. Values
out of range are refused, not clamped.

Merged on top of #37 and #40. The Infomarchy.qml resolve ceiling conflict with
#40 was taken as a union (26 + 4 + 2 = 32). 435 tests pass on the merged tree.
First contribution from this author.

Note on the handle: GitHub has no X field and no social accounts, and
shieldsworks.com links no X profile. Ask before tagging.

### FLEET sessions: which remote agent needs you, and one click to get there (#37)

**RidgetopAi (Brian)** · GitHub [@RidgetopAi](https://github.com/RidgetopAi) · X [@RidgetopAI](https://x.com/RidgetopAI) · ridgetopai.net

Builds on #35. A fleet host running Infomarchy now expands its FLEET row into
one line per remote session: project, working or idle, and a NEEDS YOU tag, with
the card glowing when any remote agent is waiting. Clicking a row opens a
terminal, ssh's over and lands in that exact tmux window and pane. A host
without bun or Infomarchy keeps its plain ps row and is asked again only every
10 minutes.

Privacy boundary: only provider, project basename, attention state, busy, stale,
uptime and the tmux address leave the remote machine. Window titles, prompt
text, paths and git state do not. The remote builds the row in one function and
the receiver validates it again. Checked live on gus: the payload carried exactly
those fields and nothing else.

Merged on top of #40. 430 tests pass on the merged tree. First contribution from
this author.

Note on the handle: on 2026-09-22 GitHub carried no X field and no social
accounts. Re-checked 2026-09-26 and both now declare @RidgetopAI, with
ridgetopai.net as the site; the account exists. Verified, not guessed.

### The desk keeps clear of the bar on whichever edge it occupies (#40)

**Danny Welch** · GitHub [@dannyowelch](https://github.com/dannyowelch) · X [@dannyowelch](https://x.com/dannyowelch)

The cards used to reserve a fixed 40px strip at the top, because the background
layer ignores exclusion zones. A bottom or side bar covered the desk, and hiding
the bar left the gap behind. The desk now reads the live bar from the shell API
and clears only the edge the bar is on, by the bar's real thickness. Moving,
resizing or hiding the bar moves the cards immediately, with no reload.

Merged 9a47cce. 390 tests pass on the merged tree. First contribution from this
author.

Note on the handle: GitHub carries no X link and no social accounts. The X
account @dannyowelch has the same display name (Danny Welch), replies to
@NixFred directly, and posts about running Omarchy, so it counts as verified,
not guessed.

